{"id": 119175, "acmi_id": "B2003857", "title": "Grand Steeple Chase de Paris 1922", "title_annotation": "", "slug": "grand-steeple-chase-de-paris-1922", "creator_credit": "Pathe Films", "credit_line": "", "headline_credit": "Paris/France, 1922", "record_type": "work", "type": "Film", "is_on_display": false, "last_on_display_place": null, "last_on_display_date": null, "is_context_indigenous": false, "material_description": "", "unpublished": false, "external": false, "first_production_date": "1922-01-01T10:00:00+10:00", "commissioned": false, "brief_description": "<p>The John Robertson Duigan Collection is a collection of silent 9.5mm home movies filmed by early aviator and engineer John Robertson Duigan (1882–1951). The collection includes a Pathé-Baby 9.5mm film camera and projector owned by Duigan. The home movies provide an insight into the everyday lives of John and his family in Victoria, including picnics, trips to the Grampians and Colac, family snapshots and aeroplanes of the late 1920s.</p>\n<p>This is a French Pathé Baby film, originally presented on 9.5mm film, ‘Grand Steeple Chase de Paris 1922’ from John Robertson Duigan&#8217;s collection.</p>", "constellations_primary": [], "constellations_other": [], "recommendations": [], "title_for_label": "<p>Grand Steeple Chase de Paris 1922</p>", "creator_credit_for_label": "<p>Pathe Films</p>", "headline_credit_for_label": "<p>Paris/France, 1922</p>", "description": "<p>The John Robertson Duigan Collection is a collection of silent 9.5mm home movies filmed by early aviator and engineer John Robertson Duigan (1882–1951). The collection includes a Pathé-Baby 9.5mm film camera and projector owned by Duigan. The home movies provide an insight into the everyday lives of John and his family in Victoria, including picnics, trips to the Grampians and Colac, family snapshots and aeroplanes of the late 1920s.</p>\n<p>This is a French Pathé Baby film, originally presented on 9.5mm film, ‘Grand Steeple Chase de Paris 1922’ from John Robertson Duigan&#8217;s collection.</p>", "description_for_label": ["<p>The John Robertson Duigan Collection is a collection of silent 9.5mm home movies filmed by early aviator and engineer John Robertson Duigan (1882–1951). The collection includes a Pathé-Baby 9.5mm film camera and projector owned by Duigan. The home movies provide an insight into the everyday lives of John and his family in Victoria, including picnics, trips to the Grampians and Colac, family snapshots and aeroplanes of the late 1920s.</p>\n<p>This is a French Pathé Baby film, originally presented on 9.5mm film, ‘Grand Steeple Chase de Paris 1922’ from John Robertson Duigan&#8217;s collection.</p>"], "credit_line_for_label": "", "details": [{"label": "Duration", "display_values": ["00:02:16:00"]}, {"label": "Subject categories", "display_values": ["Archival, Cinemagazines & Newsreels", "Archival, Cinemagazines & Newsreels&nbsp;→ Newsreels - France", "Hobbies, Recreation & Sport&nbsp;→ Horse racing", "Short films"]}, {"label": "Sound/audio", "display_values": ["Silent"]}, {"label": "Colour", "display_values": ["Black and White"]}], "stats": {"tap_count": 0}, "links": [], "creators_primary": [{"id": 1898915, "name": "Pathe Films", "creator_id": 36669, "creator_wikidata_id": null, "role": "creator", "role_id": 968, "is_primary": true}], "creators_other": [], "video_links": [{"id": 1416, "name": "ACMI External Digital Access Copy", "uri": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AoIlrYdyC_E"}], "media_note": null, "holdings": [{"name": "9.5mm film; Master", "identifier": "", "description": ""}, {"name": "MOV file ProRes4444; Digital Preservation Master - overscan", "identifier": "", "description": ""}, {"name": "MOV file ProRes4444; Digital Preservation Master - presentation", "identifier": "", "description": ""}, {"name": "MPEG-4 Digital File; ACMI Digital Access Copy - overscan", "identifier": "", "description": ""}, {"name": "MPEG-4 Digital File; ACMI Digital Access Copy - presentation", "ident